# MarkItDown usage (optional)

MarkItDown MCP/CLI is **opt-in**. Do not call it on every chat.

## When to use

- User invokes `/markitdown`, or attaches/asks about PDF, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, or similar Office docs
- Bank specs, mapping sheets, BRDs that need structured Markdown before reasoning

## When not to use

- Applogs (use `bob shrink-logs`)
- Source code, Flyway, processors
- Jira / Confluence (Atlassian MCP)
- RCA greps / Plan gate text

## How

1. Prefer MCP tool `convert_to_markdown` if server `markitdown` is enabled.
2. Else CLI: `python C:/Users/ashutosh.kumar/.cursor/tools/markitdown-shim/cli.py "<abs-path>"`
3. Keep converted Markdown off the hot path when huge - summarize; write to a file if needed.
